Revert upstream 6eabf2242 and 8d2f5d6ea (MTGS early vsync)

8d2f5d6ea lets the EE run on to the next frame as soon as its vsync is
consumed, so a finished frame can be presented from a ring drain outside
retro_run. With RetroArch on Vulkan that makes the full-screen input
overlay (the Sinden light gun border) get drawn inside the game viewport
for single frames, roughly every 0.75 s - a visible border flicker in
every PS2 light gun game. 6eabf2242 is upstream's follow-up fix for a
hang on content close that 8d2f5d6ea introduced, so both go together.

Measured on the box (grim captures): unreverted core about 1 bad frame
in 60, this revert 0 in 600. Drop when upstream no longer needs it.

Only the source hunks are reverted; the tests/mtgsvsync and
tests/mtgsclose harnesses the commits added are not part of the build.

